    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When first platted in 1882, the town was called Marathon before adopting the name Earling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/earling_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1928, a 23‑day exorcism of Anna Ecklund at a local convent drew national attention to Earling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earling%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "That exorcism inspired William Peter Blatty’s 1971 novel The Exorcist and its 1973 film adaptation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/earling_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mosquito Creek rises just north of Earling, adding a small watershed to the town’s landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
